ns: org creation, member role changes, file uploads, policy violations. Log to immutable storage (append-only file or audit database).\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalNotes\": {\n    \"strengths\": [\n      \"✓ Tenant isolation enforced at ORM level (ZenStack policies) rather than application logic\",\n      \"✓ Better-auth is a mature, well-maintained library for auth\",\n      \"✓ API responses use typed error envelopes with codes (not raw SQL/stack traces)\",\n      \"✓ WebSocket messages use a typed contract (realtime-events.ts)\",\n      \"✓ Database access abstracted through `db.*` operators (prevents direct SQL exposure)\",\n      \"✓ Environment variables validated at startup (src/env.ts)\",\n      \"✓ Policy tests exist and should catch many tenant isolation bugs\"\n    ],\n    \"blindSpots\": [\n      \"⚠ Minified production code is unauditable for client-side logic bugs\",\n      \"⚠ Backend code not provided; cannot verify auth routes, database policies, rate limiting implementation\",\n      \"⚠ No visibility into CI/CD security (dependency scanning, SAST, secrets scanning)\",\n      \"⚠ Cannot verify Redis or cluster configuration for multi-instance deployments\",\n      \"⚠ Email handling (Resend API) security not visible; verify API keys are never logged\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Key Security Concerns\n\n### **Priority 1: Tenant Isolation** (✓ Architecture looks sound, needs testing)\nThe AGENTS.md states this is \"the most important invariant.\" ZenStack enforces policies at the ORM level. **Verification required**: Run `apps/api/tests/policies.test.ts` and expand with additional adversarial tests (cross-tenant data access, permission escalation).\n\n### **Priority 2: Rich Text XSS** (⚠ Cannot audit minified code)\nThe component `rich-text-Bkev6nic.js` renders user-generated content. This is a common XSS vector. **Action**: Verify the underlying implementation uses a sanitization library and test with OWASP XSS payloads.\n\n### **Priority 3: CSRF Protection** (⚠ Not visible in minified code)\nAPI uses cookie-based auth. **Action**: Confirm backend sets `SameSite=Strict` on session cookies and validates CSRF tokens for state-changing endpoints.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Run full security audit on unminified backend code** (`apps/api/src/`) — focus on:\n   - Better-auth route handlers\n   - Database policy enforcement\n   - File upload validation\n   - WebSocket authentication\n\n2. **Penetration testing** — specifically:\n   - Tenant isolation (attempt cross-org data access)\n   - Authentication bypass (JWT tampering, session fixation)\n   - File upload exploitation\n   - Rate limiting bypass\n\n3. **Dependency scanning** — run `npm audit` / `bun check` for known vulnerabilities\n\n4. **OWASP Top 10 checklist** — verify each control (injection, broken auth, XSS, broken access control, etc.)\n",
